# Declared exceptions to the client-data check in כלים/verify-docs.sh
# One extended regex per line, matched against "file:line:content".
#
# These are the pinned identifiers used by the scenario fixtures. They are
# synthetic by construction - repeating digits, or sequential company
# numbers - and they exist so the constraints can be exercised without a
# single real client ever entering the repository.
#
# Each value is listed explicitly on purpose. A pattern broad enough to
# cover "any nine digits in a seed file" would also cover the first real
# client number someone pastes in, and that is the one failure on this
# list that cannot be undone once it reaches a remote.
#
# Adding a line here is a decision. Write down why.

# Scenario clients - repeating-digit national ID numbers
0111111112?
022222222
033333333
044444444
055555555
066666666
077777777
088888888

# Scenario companies - sequential registration numbers
51400000[0-9]
55700000[0-9]

# Artefacts of migration timestamps read as identifiers
914000003
934000003

# Scenario contact channels - synthetic phone numbers in the smoke tests
053987654[0-9]
05[0-9]{8}.*תרחיש

# Yitzhak's own GitHub account name, which appears in project notes.
# NOTE: the account name embeds his phone number. That is his own data,
# not a client's, and it is already public on GitHub - but it is worth
# knowing that the username reveals it.
m0556742573
05212345[0-9]
